      "ownership_topology": {
        "candidate": "One spawn_task_on Task<uint64_t> per worker owns an allocator-backed coroutine frame, TaskDriver, JoinState and pooled guarded Fiber stack; the external owner retains and joins four move-only JoinHandles",
        "peer": "One pre-v6 Task<uint64_t> per worker is caller-owned, spawn_detached_on retains its runtime Fiber, one caller-owned typed slot preserves the result and one WaitGroup provides each task's join completion",
        "equivalence": "Both persistent routes exclude scheduler/task construction, perform 256 warmups then the same 4096 externally acknowledged four-worker episodes, preserve exact owner on publication and wake, return the same typed checksums, wait each task to completion and charge result publication plus join"
